    "biography": "Employed at the CNR-ISPA by 1998. Currently senior researcher principally involved in the improvement of food quality and nutritional value by the application of microbial biotechnologies. Her research activities are aimed at improving the quality and safety of foods through the use and optimization of microbial biotechnologies, including fermentation of cereal and vegetable matrices, using microbial strains with peculiar technological and probiotic characteristics. Application of microbiological and chemical methodologies (HPLC), uni- and multivariate statistical analysis. She engages in national and international projects/collaborations."
